am Heart Study</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2002</year><volume>106</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12119250</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/01.CIR.0000022663.26468.5B</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Polak</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Chazaro</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Cupples</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolf</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Agostino</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Donnell</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic and environmental contributions to atherosclerosis phenotypes in men and women: heritability of carotid intima-media thickness in the Framingham Heart Study</article-title><source>Stroke</source><year>2003</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>401</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12574549</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1161/01.STR.0000048214.56981.6F</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murabito</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Guo</surname><given-names>C-Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Agostino</surname><given-names>RB</given-names><suffix>Sr</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Genetic Contributions to Peripheral Arterial Disease: Heritability of the Ankle-Brachial Blood Pressure Index in the Framingham Heart Study</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>164</volume><fpage>963</fpage><lpage>968</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16928729</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/aje